<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<archimate:model xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:archimate="http://www.archimatetool.com/archimate" name="Hatherley Plate Ltd" id="id-5d68c822a1104247a8cf825c07e9f9b3" version="5.0.0">
  <folder name="Strategy" id="id-b5319f0d6fef41c2bd944a1d5c0508be" type="strategy">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Promise" id="id-9c2c1a6a78f0475681b48889b2664099">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - View Plan Job 02 approved; plant-brief.md sales-to-mill chain
Organisational ability to commit a plate date to a customer before mill work is locked. Sales-facing; OrderSight remains the sales-facing system for this capability (wording only, not modelled as an application here).</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Order" id="id-f6c7c6a74874412ba24c60d318292ad2">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - View Plan Job 02 approved; plant-brief.md sales-to-mill chain
Organisational ability to hold one customer order identity through sales and works-order handoff so promise and mill schedule talk about the same order. WorksERP stays works-order context; no ERP replacement.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Mill schedule" id="id-ed34ec1744a1458b9f7e1579932f2af6">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - View Plan Job 02 approved; plant-brief.md Named as-is systems
Organisational ability to plan and run the mill week for plate orders. MillOS owns this capability as mill schedule system of record (ownership in documentation only; no application element on this view).</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Collect" id="id-50f22633aea34b3b8536e05a14fda533">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - View Plan Job 02 approved; plant-brief.md sales-to-mill chain
Organisational ability to close the loop after mill work so sales and plant can see what left the mill against the same order identity used at promise.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Business" id="id-231a6d672e0e48869c8e7e5569437ca3" type="business">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessRole" name="Plant Manager" id="id-c2d53b4de0d44d7c92f5e4ea51332ccf">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Roles; View Plan canvas audience
Business role that owns plant operations at Hatherley Works and needs the promise-to-rolling chain readable without inventing systems.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessRole" name="Head of Sales" id="id-a10b3ee5bc3c49088e973710f1b8397e">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Roles; View Plan canvas audience
Business role that owns customer promises and needs the same chain visible from promise; PromiseSheet remains the pain, not a modelled application.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessRole" name="Operations Planner" id="id-7a3f4a278904406cbb3c52f2fa45825a">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Roles; View Plan canvas audience
Business role that turns promises into works orders and mill schedule so plan and promise stop diverging.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessRole" name="MES Owner" id="id-8c313bffb8d3411c8fe9dec39a89624b">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Roles; View Plan canvas audience
Business role that owns mill-side schedule and plate rolling behaviour; MillOS stays wording only this job, no MES rewrite.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Promise" id="id-c338aa0260a345ed9be332a6b9e26be9">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - View Plan Job 03 approved; plant-brief.md PromiseSheet pain
As-is step where sales commits a customer plate date. Dual tracking still lives in PromiseSheet spreadsheet; that pain stays narrative only, not an application element on this view.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Works order" id="id-69e033ce9ca242d499799db7a6b42272">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - View Plan Job 03 approved; plant-brief.md WorksERP wording
As-is step that opens plant works work against the customer order identity so the mill can schedule real plate jobs. WorksERP is wording only here.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Mill schedule" id="id-d6a875984a84411d958d73759e2ffe1a">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - View Plan Job 03 approved; plant-brief.md MillOS wording
As-is step that locks the mill week for plate orders. Mill-owned path; MillOS remains schedule system of record in narrative only this job.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Plate rolling" id="id-ed0201833e864e08ab2950d70d2994aa">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - View Plan Job 03 approved; plant-brief.md physical mill
As-is shop-floor step that runs the hot plate through the mill against the locked schedule.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Application" id="id-24e9250033c040bc9953e8b03a615d1d" type="application">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="MillOS" id="id-e74300558c24411c9ca9cf76c2d9ecd6">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Named as-is systems; View Plan Job 04 approved
MES that owns the mill schedule for plate work. Stays separate from OrderSight; CRM programme must not be drawn as the MES.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="WorksERP" id="id-45a53e69f46a4c80a0e8bcb81ba24cf9">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Named as-is systems; View Plan Job 04 approved
On-site ERP that holds works orders, invoices, and plate stock wording. Not replaced this run; no ERP replacement element.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="PromiseSheet" id="id-d5dab10f11a04eedb0ba9532bd2940b1">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Named as-is systems; View Plan Job 04 approved
Shared-drive spreadsheet that still holds customer promises. Modelled as the as-is pain system, not a target platform.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="OrderSight" id="id-b8e160d2c6d24f34badc02f1b6ae6c6f">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Named as-is systems; View Plan Job 04 approved
Sales-facing CRM in pilot, funded for visibility. Separate application from MillOS; must not swallow the MES.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="PlantGate" id="id-d0698a626afc460d8de1493b05a421e6">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Named as-is systems; View Plan Job 04 approved
Integration gateway that bridges OrderSight promises to WorksERP works orders. Does not talk to mill equipment; no equipment or node elements this job.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Technology &amp; Physical" id="id-d1f4e4be365f48ab814821d6c4ffe570" type="technology">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Mill floor node" id="id-c2b0ccf345fb4ce78c7e0687ed2fbe52">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Physical (job 5); View Plan Job 05 approved
Shop-floor compute and control locus on the plate mill floor. Hosts rolling equipment assignment; not an OrderSight host.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="On-prem app server" id="id-ef9c0f14635a4a95adb8ba9858a25df2">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Physical (job 5); View Plan Job 05 approved
On-premises application server that hosts MillOS and WorksERP for the mill path. OrderSight is deliberately not placed here.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="PlantGate node" id="id-8d9fc0f78d2b4122bb9977edc94e9305">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Physical (job 5); View Plan Job 05 approved
Node in the comms room that hosts the PlantGate integration gateway. Separate from mill-floor equipment.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Facility" name="Plate mill building" id="id-b1d315115a8249809f7750591162b405">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Physical (job 5); View Plan Job 05 approved
Single-site plate mill building at Hatherley Works. Contains the mill floor where rolling happens; not a second site.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Facility" name="Comms room" id="id-9da853906d8c4af7805ac95eca12d643">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Physical (job 5); View Plan Job 05 approved
Communications room housing PlantGate infrastructure. Kept distinct from the mill floor so CRM paths are not mistaken for MES hosting.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Equipment" name="Rolling equipment" id="id-057eb745f829482892236d1023a52c3a">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Physical (job 5); View Plan Job 05 approved
Plate rolling equipment on the mill floor. Assigned to the mill-floor node; PlantGate does not talk to this equipment.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Motivation" id="id-aefd3f54daa04bb7aac3c92b6c85b0ad" type="motivation">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="Plant Manager" id="id-0260a5aa995b41c7b84d93d3541592c0">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Roles; View Plan Stakeholders
Owns plant operations at Hatherley Works. Needs a weekly on-mill answer without reading PromiseSheet, and keeps mill systems under plant control.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="Head of Sales" id="id-988afa0e45894cd3a657ac9c7085ed98">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Roles; View Plan Stakeholders
Owns customer promises. Needs the same weekly on-mill answer as the plant so dual tracking in PromiseSheet can stop.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="MES Owner" id="id-db0cfaa61b4048e7900b2b9bad3eea97">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Roles; View Plan Stakeholders
Owns MillOS as mill schedule system of record. Boundary witness that OrderSight must not be drawn as MillOS replacement.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="CRM Programme Manager" id="id-92664a6b007b411d979d63c25480a38c">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Roles; View Plan Stakeholders
Owns OrderSight pilot scope. Keeps the funded fix sales-facing visibility; resists expansion into mill rewrite.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="Operations Planner" id="id-ee9aa7f5d13c4ec9ba9da957d3768ed2">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Roles; View Plan Stakeholders
Plans mill work from orders. Needs one order identity from promise through schedule so plan and promise stop diverging.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="Integration Lead" id="id-9fc4203ce6ac494fbe546220c92f44b9">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Roles; View Plan Stakeholders
Owns cross-system identity and PlantGate boundary work. Shared identity without merging MillOS into OrderSight.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Driver" name="Promised plate dates do not match mill reality" id="id-fcf6a7e660504afaa4580a9a92e062d9">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Motivation spine; View Plan Technical Hints
Sales tracks customer promises in PromiseSheet while the mill schedule lives in MillOS, so promised plate dates drift from what the mill can actually run.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Goal" name="Sales and mill share one order identity from promise to schedule" id="id-77f9fed68144498386bf15c188fc2d21">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Motivation spine; View Plan Technical Hints
Desired state: one shared order identity links sales promise to mill schedule end to end, without merging systems into a single blob.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Outcome" name="Plant Manager and Head of Sales answer on-mill-this-week without PromiseSheet" id="id-bbf70387a3014a0bac693ecca4cce026">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Motivation spine; View Plan Technical Hints
Plant Manager and Head of Sales can answer whether an order is on the mill this week without opening PromiseSheet.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="OrderSight must not swallow MillOS" id="id-8387c0d7776b46b8a08ee1ad05bd0953">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Motivation spine and Hard freeze; View Plan Technical Hints
Hard boundary: OrderSight stays sales-facing visibility; MillOS remains the mill schedule system of record. Named systems appear here as wording only, not as application elements on this view.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
