      <documentation>Evidence: stated - plant-brief.md Motivation spine; View Plan Job 01 approved

## Purpose
Sign the why for OrderSight visibility work at Hatherley Works: promised plate dates drift from mill reality, sales and mill need one order identity from promise to schedule, and OrderSight must not swallow MillOS.

## Stakeholders and Concerns
Plant Manager and Head of Sales need a weekly on-mill answer without PromiseSheet. MES Owner and CRM Programme Manager witness the OrderSight/MillOS boundary. Operations Planner and Integration Lead own shared identity from promise through schedule without merging systems.

## Viewpoint
Motivation viewpoint (overview). View name Motivation Overview.

## Questions Answered
Why change? What desired state? What hard boundary stays? Who signs and who witnesses?

## Assumptions
Named systems (MillOS, PromiseSheet, OrderSight, WorksERP, PlantGate) are wording context only on this view. No application, process, capability, or node elements belong here.

## Decisions
Shared order identity is modelled as goal/outcome language, not a merged system. Requirement freezes OrderSight as sales-facing visibility only.

## Exclusions
Capabilities, processes, applications, nodes, work packages, second site, costing, MES rewrite, WMS/TMS/data lake/ERP replacement.

## Open Questions
None on the frozen spine. Later jobs pick up application and technology layers.
</documentation>
    </element>
