      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-81102748ec9f45bf8d9a8d4ed1eb5a5e">
        <bounds x="40" y="407" width="900" height="70"/>
        <content>Freeze: OrderSight and MillOS stay separate. PlantGate bridges OrderSight promises to WorksERP works orders only and does not talk to mill equipment. No nodes this job.</content>
      </child>
      <documentation>## Purpose
Show which named applications hold and support promises, works orders, and mill schedule on the already-modelled operations chain without merging OrderSight and MillOS.

## Stakeholders and Concerns
MES Owner, CRM Programme Manager, Integration Lead, Plant Manager, and Head of Sales need holders of promise, works order, and mill schedule readable. Shared order identity across systems; PlantGate does not talk to mill equipment.

## Viewpoint
Application Usage viewpoint; view name Application Support.

## Questions Answered
Which system holds promises, works orders, and mill schedule? Do OrderSight and MillOS stay separate? What does PlantGate bridge?

## Assumptions
Job-03 processes reused; job-02 capabilities omitted from canvas; no nodes or equipment this job.

## Decisions
Five ApplicationComponents with plant-brief names; Serving links to reused processes; PlantGate bridge documented; PromiseSheet modelled as as-is pain application.

## Exclusions
Nodes, equipment, work packages, second site, costing, MES rewrite, WMS/TMS/data lake/ERP replacement, capability redraw, motivation redraw.

## Open Questions
None blocking; first generation is draft (CP-G7).
</documentation>
    </element>
